# Run in a nested lit by ../../run-inputs.test only: the loud-failure
# composite %{msil_prog_loud_O0} (plan 5.17.4) with msil-run.py options and
# program arguments. The stand-in program writes the check line's text to
# stderr and throws, so every run's transcript is the hand-written
# loud-inputs.expected.
# RUN: rm -rf %t && split-file %s %t
# REDEFINE: %{msil_srcs} = %t/main.c
# REDEFINE: %{msil_expected_rule} = windows,linux: a loud failure (plan 5.17.4)
# REDEFINE: %{msil_run_opts} = --stdin %t/input.txt
# REDEFINE: %{msil_run_args} = first --runner wsl
# RUN: %{msil_prog_loud_O0}
# LOUD: msil: error: the construct needs M99 (loud-inputs)
#--- main.c
// prog-value: 3
// prog-stderr: msil: error: the construct needs M99 (loud-inputs)
// prog-throw: System.InvalidOperationException the thrown text
#--- input.txt
4
